   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Gender that matters",
     "texto": [
      "**Same word, two genders, two meanings.** The article is the only clue: **el orden** (tidiness) and **la orden** (a command); **el capital** (money) and **la capital** (city); **el pendiente** (earring) and **la pendiente** (slope); **el frente** (front) and **la frente** (forehead); **el cometa** (comet) and **la cometa** (kite); **el coma** and **la coma**; **el editorial** (article) and **la editorial** (publisher).\n\n**Trees and fruit.** The tree is masculine, the fruit feminine: **el manzano** / **la manzana**; **el naranjo** / **la naranja**; **el cerezo** / **la cereza**.\n\n**One form for both sexes.** The article changes: **el / la testigo**, **el / la periodista**, **el / la cantante**, **el / la joven**.\n\n**One gender for both sexes.** The article does not change: **la víctima**, **la persona**, **el personaje**, **el bebé**. You say **Juan fue la víctima**.\n\n**Feminine endings.** Nouns in **-ción**, **-sión**, **-dad**, **-tad**, **-tud**, **-ez** and **-umbre** are feminine: **la costumbre**, **la timidez**, **la actitud**.\n\n**Masculine in -ma.** Many words of Greek origin: **el problema**, **el tema**, **el sistema**, **el clima**, **el idioma**, **el programa**.\n\n**Plurals.**\n\n- Words in **-s** with the stress before the last syllable do not change: **la crisis** / **las crisis**; **el análisis** / **los análisis**; **el lunes** / **los lunes**.\n- Words ending in stressed **-í** or **-ú** take **-es** or **-s**: **esquí** → **esquís** or **esquíes**.\n- The stress moves in a few: **el régimen** → **los regímenes**; **el carácter** → **los caracteres**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Gender and plural, case by case",
     "texto": [
      "- **Gender changes the meaning**: el orden / la orden, el capital / la capital, el pendiente / la pendiente, el frente / la frente, el cometa / la cometa, el coma / la coma, el editorial / la editorial.\n- **One gender for both sexes**: la víctima, el personaje.\n- **One form for both sexes**: el / la testigo, el / la periodista.\n- **Plural that does not change**: la crisis → las crisis, el análisis → los análisis.\n- **The stress moves**: régimen → regímenes."
     ],
